From: HeavyGee <gc@lockhouse.systems>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 22:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(soup): keep <render-issue> as a system-injection prefix

feat/mermaid-parse-failure-feedback carried its own inline
SYSTEM_INJECTION_PREFIXES list in cli/src/api/apiSession.ts. Upstream
since moved that classification into cli/src/claude/utils/transcriptEntry.ts,
so the layer-side list is dead code in the composed tree and the layer
merge correctly takes the base. But upstream's list does NOT carry
<render-issue>, which is the layer's own tag.

hub/src/sync/mermaid.ts wraps render hints in <render-issue> and injects
them as type:user messages. Without this prefix they are classified as
external user text, so mermaid parse-failure feedback renders in the
transcript as if the human typed it.

This lives in a heal rather than in the merge resolution because rerere
only replays files that actually conflicted. transcriptEntry.ts does not
conflict, so a hand edit there is silently discarded by the next compose.

diff --git a/cli/src/claude/utils/transcriptEntry.ts b/cli/src/claude/utils/transcriptEntry.ts
index 0070ef3a4..b361aa894 100644
--- a/cli/src/claude/utils/transcriptEntry.ts
+++ b/cli/src/claude/utils/transcriptEntry.ts
@@ -15,6 +15,10 @@ const SYSTEM_INJECTION_PREFIXES = [
     '<command-name>',
     '<local-command-caveat>',
     '<system-reminder>',
+    // Mermaid parse-failure feedback (driver/feat-mermaid-parse-failure-feedback):
+    // hub/src/sync/mermaid.ts wraps render hints in these tags and injects
+    // them as user messages, so they are bookkeeping, not human text.
+    '<render-issue>',
 ]
 
 export function extractRawUserTextContent(content: unknown): string | null {
